        {
          "id": "step-4-1",
          "claim": "By [F3]–[F4], each bond contributes $\\mathcal J(I/4-e/2)$.\nOn the quartet both swaps are $I$, so both $e$'s vanish and the total is\n$(\\mathcal J_{12}+\\mathcal J_{23})I/4$. On either doublet pair,\n$$e_{12}=\\begin{pmatrix}2&0\\\\0&0\\end{pmatrix},\\qquad e_{23}=\\begin{pmatrix}1/2&-\\sqrt3/2\\\\-\\sqrt3/2&3/2\\end{pmatrix}.$$\nTherefore the two bond matrices are\n$$\\begin{pmatrix}-3/4&0\\\\0&1/4\\end{pmatrix},\\qquad \\begin{pmatrix}0&\\sqrt3/4\\\\\\sqrt3/4&-1/2\\end{pmatrix},$$\nand their real-coupled sum is the displayed doublet matrix, identical for\n$+$ and $-$. For $a=\\mathcal J_{12}$ and $b=\\mathcal J_{23}$, its trace is\n$-(a+b)/2$ and determinant is $-3(a-b)^2/16$; solving the quadratic\ncharacteristic equation gives\n$-(a+b)/4\\pm\\frac12\\sqrt{a^2-ab+b^2}$. This proves the exact block\ndecomposition and multiplicity of these eigenvalues.",
          "step": "4.1",
          "inputs": [
            "F3",
            "F4",
            "step 2.2",
            "algebra"
          ]
        }
      ],
