      "supplier_excerpts": [
        {
          "supplier": "def-nrqmx-spin-half-tensor-chain",
          "carrier": "items/def-nrqmx-spin-half-tensor-chain.md",
          "status": "Current draft supplier interface inspected.",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "exact_statement": "Let $N\\geq1$ be an integer. The finite spin-half tensor chain is the complex\ninner-product space\n$$\\mathcal H_N:=(\\mathbb C^2)^{\\otimes N}$$\nwith the standard tensor-product inner product, linear in its first argument.\nFix the standard orthonormal basis $|0\\rangle,|1\\rangle$ of $\\mathbb C^2$.\nLet $\\sigma^x,\\sigma^y,\\sigma^z$ be the Pauli matrices of the finite-spin\nmatrix supplier, and for $1\\leq k\\leq N$ define\n$$\\sigma_k^a:=I^{\\otimes(k-1)}\\otimes\\sigma^a\\otimes I^{\\otimes(N-k)},\\qquad J_k^a:=\\tfrac12\\sigma_k^a\\quad(a\\in\\{x,y,z\\}).$$\nFor $1\\leq i<N$, define the adjacent swap $s_i$ on elementary tensors by\n$$s_i(v_1\\otimes\\cdots\\otimes v_N):=v_1\\otimes\\cdots\\otimes v_{i+1}\\otimes v_i\\otimes\\cdots\\otimes v_N.$$\nWrite\n$$|\\omega\\rangle:=\\tfrac1{\\sqrt2}(|0\\rangle\\otimes|1\\rangle-|1\\rangle\\otimes|0\\rangle),\\qquad P_i:=I^{\\otimes(i-1)}\\otimes P_\\omega\\otimes I^{\\otimes(N-i-1)},$$\nwhere $P_\\omega v:=\\langle v,\\omega\\rangle\\,\\omega$ on the adjacent two\nfactors. Also put $e_i:=I_{\\mathcal H_N}-s_i$ for $1\\leq i<N$. If $N=1$,\nthese bond-indexed families are empty.\n\nThis is a mathematical definition of finite-dimensional tensor spaces and\noperators; it makes no physical claim about a material, a particle species, or\nan adopted statistics sector.",
          "relevant_hypotheses_and_conventions": "[F1] [[def-nrqmx-spin-half-tensor-chain]],\n[[thm-tensor-product-basis-from-bases]]: the eight binary tensor words form a\nbasis of $\\mathcal H_3$; $\\sigma_j^a$ acts by the Pauli matrix on factor $j$.",
          "supplier_proof_status": "Current Step-1 draft definition and exact interface inspected; proof is not applicable.",
          "consumer_use": "F1 supplies this interface in step(s) 1.1."
        },
        {
          "supplier": "thm-nrqmx-spin-half-temperley-lieb",
          "carrier": "items/thm-nrqmx-spin-half-temperley-lieb.md",
          "status": "Current draft supplier interface inspected.",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "exact_statement": "Let $N\\geq1$, $\\mathcal H_N=(\\mathbb C^2)^{\\otimes N}$ with the standard\northonormal basis $|0\\rangle,|1\\rangle$ on each factor, and for\n$1\\leq i<N$ define $s_i$ to swap factors $i,i+1$. Put\n$|\\omega\\rangle=(|01\\rangle-|10\\rangle)/\\sqrt2$,\n$P_\\omega v=\\langle v,\\omega\\rangle\\omega$, let $P_i$ act as $P_\\omega$ on\nfactors $i,i+1$ and identity on all others, and set $e_i=I-s_i$. For every\nbond,\n$$e_i=I-s_i=2P_i,\\qquad e_i^*=e_i,\\qquad e_i^2=2e_i.$$\nFor $1\\leq i<N-1$,\n$$e_i e_{i+1}e_i=e_i,\\qquad e_{i+1}e_i e_{i+1}=e_{i+1},$$\nand $e_i e_j=e_j e_i$ when $|i-j|>1$. Consequently the assignment\n$u_i\\mapsto e_i$ defines a star-preserving algebra representation\n$$P_N(\\mathbb C,2)\\longrightarrow\\operatorname{End}(\\mathcal H_N).$$\nFor $\\lambda\\vdash N$ with at most two rows, put\n$M_\\lambda=\\operatorname{Hom}_{S_N}(S^\\lambda,\\mathcal H_N)$ and use the\nunitary Schur–Weyl decomposition\n$\\mathcal H_N\\cong\\bigoplus_{\\lambda\\vdash N,\\,\\ell(\\lambda)\\le2}\nS^\\lambda\\otimes M_\\lambda$. Each $e_i$ acts on the Specht factor as\n$I-\\rho_\\lambda((i,i+1))$ and as identity on the multiplicity factor. No\nfaithfulness assertion is made.",
          "relevant_hypotheses_and_conventions": "[F3] [[thm-nrqmx-spin-half-temperley-lieb]]: on three sites,\n$e_{12}=I-s_{12}$ and $e_{23}=I-s_{23}$; these are the loop-weight-two\nTemperley–Lieb generators.",
          "supplier_proof_status": "Current Step-1 draft statement and complete proof inspected in this batch; independent acceptance is not asserted.",
          "consumer_use": "F3 supplies this interface in step(s) 3.1."
        },
        {
          "supplier": "thm-nrqmx-heisenberg-exchange-tl",
          "carrier": "items/thm-nrqmx-heisenberg-exchange-tl.md",
          "status": "Current draft supplier interface inspected.",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "exact_statement": "Let $N\\geq1$, let $\\hbar>0$, and let real couplings\n$\\mathcal J_i\\in\\mathbb R$ be given for $1\\leq i<N$. On\n$\\mathcal H_N=(\\mathbb C^2)^{\\otimes N}$, let $\\sigma_i^a$ be the Pauli\nmatrix $\\sigma^a$ acting on factor $i$ and identity on all other factors,\nwhere\n$$\\sigma^x=\\begin{pmatrix}0&1\\\\1&0\\end{pmatrix},\\quad \\sigma^y=\\begin{pmatrix}0&-i\\\\i&0\\end{pmatrix},\\quad \\sigma^z=\\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\\\0&-1\\end{pmatrix}.$$\nLet $s_i$ swap factors $i,i+1$ and put $e_i=I-s_i$. Set\n$S_i^a:=\\hbar\\sigma_i^a/2$ for $a\\in\\{x,y,z\\}$, and define the finite-chain\noperator\n$$H:=\\sum_{i=1}^{N-1}\\mathcal J_i\\hbar^{-2}\\sum_{a=x,y,z}S_i^aS_{i+1}^a.$$\nFor every bond,\n$$\\hbar^{-2}\\sum_a S_i^aS_{i+1}^a=\\tfrac12s_i-\\tfrac14I =\\tfrac14I-\\tfrac12e_i.$$\nThus $H=\\sum_i\\mathcal J_i(\\tfrac14I-\\tfrac12e_i)$ is self-adjoint, belongs\nto the represented Temperley–Lieb algebra, and on each summand of the unitary\ndecomposition\n$$\\mathcal H_N\\cong\\bigoplus_{\\lambda\\vdash N,\\,\\ell(\\lambda)\\le2} S^\\lambda\\otimes M_\\lambda,\\qquad M_\\lambda:=\\operatorname{Hom}_{S_N}(S^\\lambda,\\mathcal H_N),$$\nacts on $S^\\lambda$ and as identity on $M_\\lambda$. For $N=1$ the sum is\nempty and $H=0$.",
          "relevant_hypotheses_and_conventions": "[F4] [[thm-nrqmx-heisenberg-exchange-tl]]: a real-coupled finite chain has\nthe exact bond identity $S_i\\cdot S_{i+1}/\\hbar^2=I/4-e_i/2$.",
          "supplier_proof_status": "Current Step-1 draft statement and complete proof inspected in this batch; independent acceptance is not asserted.",
          "consumer_use": "F4 supplies this interface in step(s) 3.1."
        },
        {
          "supplier": "prop-nrqm-orbital-and-spin-finite-spin-matrices",
          "carrier": "items/prop-nrqm-orbital-and-spin-finite-spin-matrices.md",
          "status": "Current published supplier interface inspected.",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "exact_statement": "Let $s\\in\\frac12\\mathbb N=\\{0,\\tfrac12,1,\\tfrac32,\\dots\\}$, put $N:=2s\\in\\mathbb N$ and let\n$V_s:=\\mathbb C^{N+1}$ carry the standard inner product\n$\\langle z,w\\rangle=\\sum_{k=0}^{N}z_k\\overline{w_k}$, linear in the first argument\n([[def-inner-product-space]]). Write $(e_m)_{-s\\le m\\le s}$ for the standard basis, indexed so that\n$e_m$ is the vector with entry $1$ in position $k=s-m$ and entry $0$ elsewhere; thus\n$\\langle e_m,e_n\\rangle=1$ if $m=n$ and $\\langle e_m,e_n\\rangle=0$ otherwise. Define $\\mathbb C$-linear maps\n$J_z,J_+,J_-\\in\\operatorname{End}_{\\mathbb C}(V_s)$ by their values on this basis ([[def-linear-map]]):\n\n$$J_ze_m:=m\\,e_m,\\qquad J_+e_m:=\\sqrt{(s-m)(s+m+1)}\\,e_{m+1},\\qquad J_-e_m:=\\sqrt{(s+m)(s-m+1)}\\,e_{m-1},$$\n\nwhere $e_{s+1}:=0$ and $e_{-s-1}:=0$, and put\n\n$$J_x:=\\tfrac12(J_++J_-),\\qquad J_y:=\\tfrac1{2i}(J_+-J_-),\\qquad J^2:=J_x^2+J_y^2+J_z^2 .$$\n\nThen:\n\n(a) $J_z$, $J_x$ and $J_y$ are self-adjoint endomorphisms of $V_s$\n([[def-self-adjoint-and-normal-endomorphism]]), and $J_+^*=J_-$, $J_-^*=J_+$\n([[def-adjoint-of-a-linear-map-between-inner-product-spaces]]);\n\n(b) on $V_s$ the commutators are\n\n$$[J_z,J_+]=J_+,\\qquad [J_z,J_-]=-J_-,\\qquad [J_+,J_-]=2J_z,\\qquad [J_x,J_y]=iJ_z,\\qquad [J_y,J_z]=iJ_x,\\qquad [J_z,J_x]=iJ_y ;$$\n\n(c) $J^2=J_-J_++J_z^2+J_z=J_+J_-+J_z^2-J_z=s(s+1)I$, and $[J^2,J_z]=[J^2,J_\\pm]=0$;\n\n(d) the matrix elements of the raising operator are\n$\\|J_+e_m\\|^2=(s-m)(s+m+1)$ and $\\|J_-e_m\\|^2=(s+m)(s-m+1)$, and\n$\\langle J_+e_m,e_{m+1}\\rangle=\\sqrt{(s-m)(s+m+1)}$, which is nonzero exactly when $m<s$;\n\n(e) for $s=\\tfrac12$, identify $V_{\\frac12}=\\mathbb C^2$ with the basis ordered as $(e_{\\frac12},e_{-\\frac12})$ and let\n\n$$\\sigma_x:=\\begin{pmatrix}0&1\\\\1&0\\end{pmatrix},\\qquad \\sigma_y:=\\begin{pmatrix}0&-i\\\\ i&0\\end{pmatrix},\\qquad \\sigma_z:=\\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\\\0&-1\\end{pmatrix}$$\n\nbe the Pauli matrices. Then $J_i=\\tfrac12\\sigma_i$ for $i=x,y,z$, $\\sigma_x^2=\\sigma_y^2=\\sigma_z^2=I$,\n$\\sigma_x\\sigma_y=i\\sigma_z$, $\\sigma_y\\sigma_z=i\\sigma_x$, $\\sigma_z\\sigma_x=i\\sigma_y$, and consequently\n$\\sigma_i\\sigma_j+\\sigma_j\\sigma_i=2\\delta_{ij}I$ and $\\sigma_i\\sigma_j=\\delta_{ij}I+i\\sum_k\\varepsilon_{ijk}\\sigma_k$ for all $i,j$, where $\\delta_{ij}=1$ if $i=j$ and $0$ otherwise, and $\\varepsilon_{ijk}=0$ when two of $i,j,k$ coincide, and otherwise $\\varepsilon_{ijk}$ is the sign of the permutation $(x,y,z)\\mapsto(i,j,k)$; the sum ranges over $k\\in\\{x,y,z\\}$. The same convention with indices $1,2,3$ uses the order-preserving relabelling $(1,2,3)=(x,y,z)$.\n\nAll statements are finite-dimensional linear algebra: no physical interpretation of $J_x,J_y,J_z$ as angular momentum, and no measurement postulate, is asserted here.",
          "relevant_hypotheses_and_conventions": "[F2] [[prop-nrqm-orbital-and-spin-finite-spin-matrices]]: in the ordered\nbasis $|0\\rangle,|1\\rangle$, $\\sigma^z|0\\rangle=|0\\rangle$,\n$\\sigma^z|1\\rangle=-|1\\rangle$, and\n$\\frac12(\\sigma^x+i\\sigma^y)|1\\rangle=|0\\rangle$,\n$\\frac12(\\sigma^x+i\\sigma^y)|0\\rangle=0$,\n$\\frac12(\\sigma^x-i\\sigma^y)|0\\rangle=|1\\rangle$,\nand $\\frac12(\\sigma^x-i\\sigma^y)|1\\rangle=0$; these raising and lowering\nmatrices are adjoints.",
          "supplier_proof_status": "Published statement and complete proof inspected; no new independent approval is asserted.",
          "consumer_use": "F2 supplies this interface in step(s) 1.2."
        },
        {
          "supplier": "thm-nrqmx-schur-weyl-exchange-blocks",
          "carrier": "items/thm-nrqmx-schur-weyl-exchange-blocks.md",
          "status": "Current draft supplier interface inspected.",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "exact_statement": "Let $d\\geq1$ and $N\\geq0$ be integers, let $V=\\mathbb C^d$ with its standard\nHermitian inner product, and give $H_N:=V^{\\otimes N}$ its standard\ntensor-product inner product. For $\\pi\\in S_N$ use the left place action\n$$\\rho(\\pi)(v_1\\otimes\\cdots\\otimes v_N):=v_{\\pi^{-1}(1)}\\otimes\\cdots\\otimes v_{\\pi^{-1}(N)},$$\nand for $U\\in U(d):=\\{A\\in M_d(\\mathbb C):A^*A=I\\}$ use the diagonal action\n$\\Delta_N(U):=U^{\\otimes N}$. For a partition $\\lambda\\vdash N$ with at most\n$d$ rows, let $S^\\lambda$ be the corresponding complex Specht module and put\n$$M_\\lambda:=\\operatorname{Hom}_{S_N}(S^\\lambda,H_N),\\qquad d_\\lambda:=\\dim_{\\mathbb C}S^\\lambda.$$\nEquip $S^\\lambda$ with any $S_N$-invariant Hermitian inner product and equip\n$M_\\lambda$ with the normalized Hilbert-Schmidt inner product\n$$\\langle f,g\\rangle_{M_\\lambda}:=d_\\lambda^{-1}\\operatorname{Tr}(g^*f).$$\nEquip each $S^\\lambda\\otimes M_\\lambda$ with the product inner product,\ndefined on elementary tensors by\n$\\langle s\\otimes f,s'\\otimes g\\rangle=\n\\langle s,s'\\rangle\\langle f,g\\rangle$ and extended sesquilinearly, and give\nthe direct sum the orthogonal direct-sum inner product.\nThen the evaluation map\n$$\\Phi:\\bigoplus_{\\lambda\\vdash N,\\ \\ell(\\lambda)\\leq d}S^\\lambda\\otimes M_\\lambda\\longrightarrow H_N,\\qquad \\Phi(s\\otimes f):=f(s),$$\nis unitary. Under this decomposition every permutation acts on $S^\\lambda$\nand as the identity on $M_\\lambda$, while every diagonal $U(d)$ action acts\nas the identity on $S^\\lambda$ and by postcomposition on $M_\\lambda$. The\nmultiplicity spaces in the sum are nonzero; partitions with more than $d$\nrows have zero multiplicity space.",
          "relevant_hypotheses_and_conventions": "[F5] [[thm-nrqmx-schur-weyl-exchange-blocks]]: permutation operators act on\nSpecht factors and collective unitary operators act on multiplicity factors.",
          "supplier_proof_status": "Current Step-1 draft statement and complete proof inspected in this batch; independent acceptance is not asserted.",
          "consumer_use": "F5 supplies this interface in step(s) 2.2."
        },
        {
          "supplier": "thm-tensor-product-basis-from-bases",
          "carrier": "items/thm-tensor-product-basis-from-bases.md",
          "status": "Current published supplier interface inspected.",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "exact_statement": "Let $R$ be a commutative ring. If $M$ is free with basis $(e_i)_{i\\in I}$ and $N$ is free with basis $(f_j)_{j\\in J}$, then $M\\otimes_RN$ is free with basis\n\n$$\\bigl(e_i\\otimes f_j\\bigr)_{(i,j)\\in I\\times J}.$$\n\nEquivalently, the canonical map $R^{(I\\times J)}\\to M\\otimes_RN$ sending the standard basis vector at $(i,j)$ to $e_i\\otimes f_j$ is an isomorphism. This includes an empty basis in either factor.",
          "relevant_hypotheses_and_conventions": "[F1] [[def-nrqmx-spin-half-tensor-chain]],\n[[thm-tensor-product-basis-from-bases]]: the eight binary tensor words form a\nbasis of $\\mathcal H_3$; $\\sigma_j^a$ acts by the Pauli matrix on factor $j$.",
          "supplier_proof_status": "Published statement and complete proof inspected; no new independent approval is asserted.",
          "consumer_use": "F1 supplies this interface in step(s) 1.1."
        }
      ],
